            <ArticleTitle>Presentation and management of late-onset duodenomegaly in a teenager with chronic obstruction from malrotation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e21-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpedsurg.2008.03.070</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anomalies of intestinal rotation typically present in infancy and early childhood. The diagnosis in older children and adults may be vague and delayed. We discuss a case and management of a patient with late-onset duodenomegaly with chronic obstruction from malrotation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
